        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Fizz, Painkiller\n- Concepts: cocktail ingredients, cocktail characteristics, serving methods\n\nFacts:\n- Fizz is defined by the use of an acidic juice such as lemon or lime and carbonated water.\n- The Painkiller is made with Pusser's rum, four parts pineapple juice, one part cream of coconut, and one part orange juice.\n- The Painkiller is shaken, served over ice, and topped with a generous amount of fresh nutmeg.",
